.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
**/__pycache__/
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.venv/
# Any virtualenv variant, including backups like .venv.py39.bak -- a committed venv is
# thousands of files of vendored, machine-specific code, and its bundled JavaScript breaks
# the lint job.
**/.venv*/
**/node_modules/
**/dist/
**/coverage/
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
pipeline/logs/
pipeline/cache/
# Downloaded payloads. Regenerable by definition, and stale on purpose once expired.
pipeline/data/cache/
# Controlled validation retains complete provider payloads locally for audit, but they are
# not redistributed with the public dashboard or committed without a provider-rights review.
pipeline/data/staging/
# The point-in-time store (pipeline/data/pit/) is deliberately NOT ignored. Scheduled runs
# happen on ephemeral runners, so committing it back is the only way the history survives -
# and it cannot be reconstructed later, because the providers only ever serve today.
